WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.200
Maybe after binge watching every episode of "Two Cents" you finally decided to make some big changes.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.530
You looked your debts right in the eye and
made a plan to pay them off in 10 years.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.020
You budgeted your household spending, and
even started setting aside funds for retirement.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:20.280
For the first time in your life, you feel
like you’re really in control of your own future.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.160
But there’s still one financial storm brewing
that might not be on your radar.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:32.250
A money monster growing in your closet that
even the bravest budgeter has trouble facing…

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.540
your parents.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.660
In many cultures, it’s normal and expected
that younger generations take care of their

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.170
parents in their old age.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.500
But during 20th century America, pensions,
social security, and other retirement plans

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.890
made it possible to remain independent throughout
one’s autumn years.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.989
These days, however, with pensions in decline
and stagnant wage growth making saving for

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:06.830
retirement even harder, seniors find themselves
caught between cultural expectations of self-reliance

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.510
and economic reality.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.760
More than a third of people over 55 have no
retirement savings at all.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.830
And only 13% have made any written retirement
plans.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:22.280
If you care at all about your parents’ well-being,
this could very well be your problem, too.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.860
Unfortunately, as we’ve mentioned in a previous
video, parents and kids don’t talk to each

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.380
other about money very much.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.549
It can be especially awkward when the roles
are reversed.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:35.591
Parents don’t like to feel like a burden
and kids don’t like to think about their

00:01:35.591 --> 00:01:37.040
parents needing help.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.520
So it’s very common for adult children to
get blindsided by Mom or Dad’s dire financial straits.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.960
There are enough unpredictable money problems in the world.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.080
This doesn’t have to be one of them!

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.560
But it does mean that you’ll have to find
a way to initiate the conversation.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.090
You could just blurt out “Hey guys!

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.280
Am I gonna have to support you at some point?”

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.670
Or, if you want a more delicate approach,
you can start by asking them to create a “Just

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:06.200
In Case” document, which outlines where
their assets are located and the contact information

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.070
of any advisers or attorneys.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:12.760
By going over such a document with them, you
should start to get an idea of their overall

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.310
financial situation.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.599
The best case scenario is that they’re in
great shape!

00:02:16.599 --> 00:02:19.780
Their retirement is funded and they’re even
planning on leaving something behind for you

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.780
and your siblings.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.420
Even in this situation, it’s good to have
the talk.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.360
Plenty of families are torn apart by estate
squabbles that could’ve been avoided with

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.730
clear communication.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:33.320
Or perhaps your parents have enough to live off of--as long as nothing goes wrong!

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:38.220
In that case, you might offer to help them
understand their Medicare options or shop around

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.340
for long-term care insurance.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.530
If the situation is worse than that--and you
are the only thing standing between them and

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.180
poverty--you have to consider what kind of
assistance will be the most effective.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:54.040
Direct gifts of cash are not always a good
idea--they can create discomfort, and might

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.319
not even be effective if your parent has a
historically troubled relationship with money.

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.900
Instead, think about what expenses you could cover
for them, like groceries or rent or travel.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.480
After all, they fed and housed and chauffeured
you around when you were little, now you’re

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.699
just returning the favor!

00:03:09.699 --> 00:03:13.760
But before you commit any dollars, you’ve
got to be sure you can afford it.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.249
Amongst people who are financially supporting
their parents, the average amount of non-mortgage

00:03:18.249 --> 00:03:20.650
debt is $22,000.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:25.239
And over one-fifth say their assistance is
costing them their own savings.

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:30.319
Wrecking your own financial health to support
your parents will only keep the cycle of dependency

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:35.559
going, and may someday put your kids in the
same crunch you now find yourself in.

00:03:35.559 --> 00:03:40.999
Like they say in those airplane safety videos,
you’ve got to get your oxygen mask on first

00:03:40.999 --> 00:03:43.230
before you help others with theirs.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:47.120
If you’re already struggling with your own
debts, it’s strongly recommended to find

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.299
non-monetary ways of helping.

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:53.139
You could sit down with them and help them
write a budget (we made a handy video to get

00:03:53.139 --> 00:03:54.139
you started).

00:03:54.139 --> 00:03:56.819
You could volunteer to run errands or do chores
for them.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.430
Or--the big one--you could offer them a place
to live.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:04.669
65% of seniors do not fully own their homes,
so just eliminating their housing expense

00:04:04.669 --> 00:04:06.180
could make all the difference.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.510
If you find that your parents are deeply in
debt, you’ll have to judge whether it’s

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:11.980
worth it to help pay them it off.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.480
Creditors can go after estates, but not next
of kin.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:20.071
So if their debt is equal to or exceeds the
value of their estate, there are

00:04:20.071 --> 00:04:24.320
a lot better uses for your money than paying
interest on loans that will may ultimately

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.560
be forgiven.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.900
When things are this dicey, the best thing
you can do is call in professional help.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.870
A certified financial planner can look at
all the pieces of this family puzzle and help

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:39.070
you draw up a plan to achieve three major
goals: (1) ensure the comfort and health of

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:44.130
your parents, while (2) allowing you to keep
paying off your own debts and (3) saving for

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.930
your own retirement.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.820
Bringing in a third party can also help defuse
tensions, so it won’t seem like a you vs.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:52.160
them situation.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:56.960
After all, maintaining a positive relationship
with your parents is still the most important thing.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.700
It’s unfortunate that talking plainly about
money is taboo in America.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:07.440
In a study done by Wells Fargo, 44% of Americans
say that talking about personal finance is

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.570
harder than talking about politics, religion
or death!

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.780
But it’s precisely that fear that lets things
fester in dark closets and eventually grow

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.120
into monsters that no one wants to face.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.730
So do your folks a solid and bring the topic
up earlier than you probably want to.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.760
Let them know that you’re on their team
and want to make sure they’re getting what

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.800
they deserve after a lifetime of hard work.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.340
They probably helped you face your monsters
as a kid, so consider it a privilege to help

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.160
them deal with theirs.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.280
And that’s our two cents!

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.060
Have you had "the talk" with your parents?

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.200
Let us know how it went in the comments.

